@ruflin brought up another issue where if we include the `data_stream` fields within the ECS component template, it may be non-useable for some use cases where they have a conflicting mapping (Filebeat?).
So what I [did](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/96171/commits/4211c3ae051c51df3e649ed687a4639aed66e794) is extract this single dynamic template into a separate component template. 

As I said before, I don't see multiple component templates as a problem, but as a use of the composable-templates feature, even if it is to workaround an issue. However, if there are objections I can revert and then the specific shippers that have such conflicts will either have to not use our ECS generic mappings, or use them and override whatever needed with explicit mappings.
